From 16a70d574413a2cc2aba6045008469f3f0f8c23e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 18:24:43 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 11/57] hw/rtc: RTC model (PIC32CM MC00), power-on-only reset
 for the 32 kHz domain

mchp-rtc (U2250): the three modes (32-bit counter with COMP0 and
MATCHCLR, 16-bit counter with PER and COMP0/1, clock/calendar with
leap years, ALARM0 and MASK0.SEL), the prescaler with PER0-7 from its
taps, compare/alarm flags on the tick after the match, COUNT/CLOCK
reads valid with COUNTSYNC/CLOCKSYNC, synchronization stalling without
CLK_RTC_OSC. Event driven on the virtual clock. The SoC picks dedicated
models by module and IP id (the JH01 RTC 03608 stays generic) and wires
the new OSC32KCTRL "rtc" output (CLK_RTC_OSC per RTCCTRL.RTCSEL) to it.

PIC32CM MC00 silicon keeps the RTC running across system resets, and
OSC32KCTRL settings too: mchp-regblock gains a por_only class flag (reset
at power-on and by SWRST only), set for the RTC and OSC32KCTRL. The rtc
test image's transcript is byte-identical between silicon and twin.

New qtest pic32cm-rtc-test.

Peripheral Pretender downstream patch; not for upstream submission.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
